    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d386">

                <pb facs="0554" n="480" sameAs="frus:frus1866p2/pg480"/>

                <head>Mr. Coggeshall to Mr.
                        Seward.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 12.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">United States Legation,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Quito,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-10-28"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >October</hi> 28, 1866</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to advise you that the
                    question of the transfer of the Gallapagos islands has been reviewed before the
                    government of Ecuador, by a proposition for their purchase from the British
                    holders of Ecuadorian bonds. Such sale direct is forbidden by the Constitution
                    of Ecuador, and by treaty stipulations, but the expediency of such a transfer,
                    at a price to be agreed upon between the contracting parties, as will put the
                    British bondholders in possession of the islands <hi rendition="#italic">de
                        facto,</hi> and yet conserve the political jurisdiction of Ecuador, has been
                    urgently presented to the cabinet of this republic, and is now, I am credibly
                    informed, a topic of official correspondence.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W. T. COGGESHALL.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, Washington, D. C</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
